# 15. AUTOMATIC COVERAGE OF FUTURE UPDATES, ADDITIONS AND CONTRIBUTIONS

### 15.1. Official Repository and Official Main Branch

For the purposes of this License, the **“Official Repository”** means the repository to which this License applies and in which this License is published by the Licensor in the root directory.

The **“Official Main Branch”** means the branch named `main` within the Official Repository.

Material committed to another branch, fork, mirror, or copy of the Official Repository shall not be included under this Section merely by reason of being present there. Such material shall become eligible for inclusion under this Section only when it is incorporated into the Official Main Branch and satisfies the other requirements of this License.

A branch replacing or succeeding `main` shall qualify as the Official Main Branch only if the Licensor expressly designates it in a dated written notice or in a revised version of this License published in the root directory of the Official Repository. Such designation shall take effect prospectively and shall not, by itself, retroactively include material that was not previously covered.

A change to the default-branch setting of the hosting platform, by itself, shall not constitute such a designation.

### 15.2. Automatic Inclusion of Future Materials

Subject to Sections 15.3, 15.4 and 15.5, the Works shall automatically include all original materials that are created, authored, or otherwise lawfully controlled by the Licensor, and that are added to, modified within, and maintained as part of the Research Collection in the Official Main Branch.

Such materials include, without limitation, updates, modifications, revisions, improvements, bug fixes, new versions, files, directories, modules, scripts, source code, software, configurations, model architectures, model weights, datasets, documentation, diagrams, tests, experimental materials, build files, and other original components.

This automatic inclusion shall also extend to future development and maintenance of existing projects, as well as to new projects and components incorporated into and maintained as part of the Research Collection in the Official Main Branch.

Each qualifying addition or modification shall become part of the Works from the date on which it is first committed to or merged into the Official Main Branch, as evidenced by the Official Repository's version-control history.

No separate file-by-file declaration, express identification, individual licensing notice, or separate release shall be required for materials that satisfy this Section.

Automatic inclusion determines only whether material falls within the scope of the Works. It does not establish that the Licensor owns or controls any rights that the Licensor does not actually possess.

### 15.3. Ownership, Rights and Contributor Contributions

A material shall be covered by this License only to the extent that the Licensor is its lawful rightsholder or has obtained all rights, permissions, assignments, and authorizations necessary to grant the permissions provided under this License.

Where any material is created or contributed by an employee, researcher, student, intern, contractor, subcontractor, independent collaborator, volunteer, or other contributor, that material shall be covered only to the extent that the necessary rights have been obtained from the actual rightsholder or from a person or entity legally authorized to grant them.

Where required, such rights shall be secured through a written assignment or written license expressly authorizing the Licensor to grant and sublicense to recipients the permissions provided under this License, within the scope and for the duration of those permissions.

Where rights may belong to an employer, university, research institution, funding body, client, commissioning party, or other organization, the necessary authorization shall be obtained from the relevant rightsholder or duly authorized entity.

The mere submission, acceptance, merging, storage, modification, or publication of a contribution in the Official Repository shall not, by itself, transfer ownership, create a license, or establish that the Licensor has the necessary authority to sublicense that contribution.

No contribution shall be represented as covered by this License to the extent that the Licensor has not obtained the rights and authority required by this Section.

### 15.4. Third-Party Materials, Datasets and Artificial Intelligence Materials

Third-Party Material remains excluded from the Works covered by this License, except to the extent expressly permitted by the applicable rights and licensing arrangements and by the provisions of this License. Its mere presence in, incorporation into, modification within, or distribution alongside the Official Repository shall not cause it to become licensed under this License.

Third-Party Material includes, without limitation, externally sourced software, libraries, code, data, datasets, text, images, documentation, model weights, pretrained models, tools, and other materials subject to rights or licensing conditions held or imposed by third parties.

The inclusion of any dataset, model, model weights, pretrained model, training data, validation data, test data, metadata, or other artificial-intelligence-related material shall not, by itself, constitute a representation or presumption that the Licensor owns or controls the underlying data, model weights, underlying works, or third-party rights associated with that material.

The Licensor's rights in original code, configurations, documentation, or other separable components shall not be construed as ownership of the third-party materials on which those components may depend or with which they may be used.

Any applicable third-party license terms, attribution requirements, usage restrictions, redistribution conditions, source-disclosure obligations, or other legally applicable conditions shall remain applicable to the relevant Third-Party Material and to any obligations that legally extend to a combined or distributed work.

Before incorporating or distributing Third-Party Material, the Licensor shall take reasonable steps to identify the applicable conditions and ensure that the contemplated use and distribution comply with them or are covered by the necessary permissions.

Where the contemplated incorporation or distribution would violate applicable third-party terms, intellectual property rights, or contractual obligations, the affected material or distribution shall not be included or carried out in that manner unless the necessary authorization is obtained or the relevant compliance requirements are otherwise satisfied.

Nothing in this License overrides, replaces, or removes rights or obligations arising from an applicable third-party license.

### 15.5. Removal, Replacement and Previously Distributed Versions

The removal, replacement, modification, or relocation of material from the Official Repository shall not, by itself, cancel or revoke permissions already validly granted under this License in respect of versions lawfully distributed or otherwise licensed before that removal, replacement, modification, or relocation.

Any such continued permissions shall remain subject to the termination provisions of this License, the terms under which they were granted, and applicable law.

This Section does not create rights that the Licensor did not possess, validate an unauthorized distribution, or cure a failure to obtain the rights required under Section 15.3 or comply with Section 15.4.

